https://doi.org/10.6028/NIST.TN.2158

https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/TechnicalNotes/NIST.TN.2158.pdf

An official technical note explaining <Charpy impact test> transition curves. Section2 describes absorbed energy, lateral expansion and fracture-appearance measures of the <ductile-to-brittle transition>.

= High-temperature Embrittlement of Stainless Steel irradiated in Fast Fluxes by A. S. Fraser and others
{c}
{parent=Materials science bibliography}
{tag=Work by A. S. Fraser}
{tag=Work by C. Cawthorne}
{title2=1966}

https://doi.org/10.1038/211291a0

Nature 211, pp.291–292. The accessible abstract discusses reduced high-temperature <ductility>, thin-foil observations of bubbles and a <helium embrittlement> mechanism involving <grain boundaries>. The abstract was inspected; the subscription-only full article was not required for the stated claim.

= Accident-tolerant fuel development awards by the United States Department of Energy
{parent=Materials science bibliography}
{c}
{title2=2019}

https://www.energy.gov/ne/articles/doe-awards-111-million-us-vendors-develop-accident-tolerant-nuclear-fuels

Program announcement describing development of doped oxide, silicide and alternative cladding concepts with work planned through 2021.

